EXT. CLIFFSIDE STAIRCASE OF THE WIND TEMPLE - DAWN

Ten thousand steps, hewn into rock. Prayer flags snap. Clouds boil below.

ALDRIC VANTERPOOL (30s, battered armor, scabbard empty) climbs, panting. Behind him, a hooded girl, THESSALY (teen, silver eyes, bare feet) hops step to step like a goat. Further down, burly SORREL IRONBARK (40s, axe on back, braided beard) hauls himself up, wheezing. Last comes the old wizard BARNABUS GLIMMERWICK (80s, crooked staff, patched robes), who rests on every third step.

ALDRIC
Barnabus, hurry!

BARNABUS
I am a wizard, not a mountain goat!

THESSALY
(skipping)
I'm a mountain goat.

SORREL
(muttering)
Gods, the stairs.

Thessaly stops at a landing. Above, a stone gate, and between its pillars, a shimmering curtain of wind. She puts out her hand. It ripples.

THESSALY
It's open.

ALDRIC
Is it safe?

THESSALY
No.

SORREL
Good. I dislike safe.

Barnabus catches up, bent double.

BARNABUS
Aldric, listen. When we cross, the Wind Warden will ask each of us one question.

ALDRIC
What question?

BARNABUS
What we fear most.

SORREL
^That's easy.

THESSALY
^That's easy.

They answer together, then glare at each other.

ALDRIC
Sorrel?

SORREL
Being forgotten.

ALDRIC
Thessaly?

THESSALY
(small)
Being found.

Aldric draws a breath. Wind howls through the gate. He steps toward it, hand on the empty scabbard.

ALDRIC
Then we go together.
